{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "Agent enrollment: from an Enrollment Code to a tailnet node",
  "description": "How an Owner's Agent joins the tailnet: the web UI issues a single-use code, the Agent's command line exchanges it for a pre-auth key, and the control plane connects to the node once it joins.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/app/agents.go",
      "line": 88,
      "title": "The Owner asks for a code",
      "description": "`func (a *Agents) IssueCode` makes a single-use Enrollment Code. Only its hash is stored, so the plain code is shown once."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/app/agents.go",
      "line": 105,
      "title": "The Agent exchanges the code",
      "description": "`func (a *Agents) Enroll` consumes the code and asks the tailnet for a pre-auth key. A code is used up even if enrolling fails afterwards."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/adapters/sqlstore/agents.go",
      "line": 22,
      "title": "Consuming a code once",
      "description": "`func (s *Store) ConsumeEnrollmentCode` marks the code used only if it is unused and unexpired, in one transaction."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/app/ports.go",
      "line": 220,
      "title": "The Tailnet port",
      "description": "`type Tailnet interface` issues keys, lists nodes, and removes a node. The control server behind it enforces who may connect to whom."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/adapters/headscale/client.go",
      "line": 50,
      "title": "The real Tailnet adapter",
      "description": "`func New(config Config) *Client` returns the Headscale adapter for the Tailnet port."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/app/fleet.go",
      "line": 55,
      "title": "The control plane connects",
      "description": "`func (f *Fleet) Reconcile` connects to every Agent whose node has joined the tailnet, and disconnects from Agents that were removed."
    }
  ]
}
